\addtocounter{subsubsection}{1}\begin{equation} \label{trivial}
\big| \log^+{|f-a|} - \log^+{|f|} \big| \leq \log^+{|a|} + \log{2}.
\end{equation}
See Hayman~\cite[Theorem~1.2]{Hayman} or Bombieri--Gubler~\cite[Theorem~13.2.10]{BombieriGubler} for the details. 
We note that $c(f,a) = f(0) - a$ when $a \neq f(0)$.

